---
import MainLayout from '../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
---

<MainLayout
  title="OmniR3 - Reliable Software Systems"
  description="Reliable, responsible, repeatable software systems built to scale."
  currentPath="/"
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container hero-wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Enterprise Software Partner</p>
      <h1>
        Reliable digital systems for teams that move fast and cannot fail.
      </h1>
      <p class="lead">
        OmniR3 designs and delivers resilient platforms, product ecosystems, and
        operational software foundations for modern organizations.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact">Start a Project</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/capabilities">Explore Capabilities</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Core Principles</p>
      <h2>The R3 framework</h2>
      <div class="cards three">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Reliable</h3>
          <p>
            Fault-tolerant architecture, robust testing, and observability-first
            engineering that perform under pressure.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Responsible</h3>
          <p>
            Secure-by-default practices, transparent governance, and clear
            ownership from discovery through delivery.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Repeatable</h3>
          <p>
            Reusable patterns, delivery playbooks, and automation that scale
            outcomes across teams and business units.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Why OmniR3</p>
        <h2>Built for growth, compliance, and speed.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cards two">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Enterprise-Grade Delivery</h3>
          <p>
            Architecture and implementation patterns aligned with security,
            scalability, and maintainability goals.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Long-Term Partnership</h3>
          <p>
            We stay engaged beyond launch to optimize performance, maintain
            quality, and support roadmap evolution.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Insights</p>
        <h2>Internal apps should be private by default.</h2>
        <p>
          Cloudflare can now attach Access to a Worker itself, covering every
          hostname and preview. That is the right default for employee-built
          tools.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/insights/workers-protected-by-access">
          Read the note
        </a>
      </div>
      <article class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">August 18, 2026</p>
        <h3>What changed</h3>
        <p>
          Access no longer has to be rebuilt for each custom domain. Policy
          follows the Worker, account-wide defaults can lock every deployment,
          and identity is available in Worker code without a homemade JWT
          check.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-band">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Ready to design your next software foundation?</h2>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact">Contact OmniR3</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</MainLayout>
